ersion":"vor","intended-application":"syndication"},{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/jap\/article-pdf\/doi\/10.1063\/1.3122599\/13758136\/034902_1_online.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,4]],"date-time":"2023-07-04T21:32:11Z","timestamp":1688506331000},"score":47.249683,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/jap\/article\/106\/3\/034902\/369987\/Pinning-at-template-feature-edges-for-step-and"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009,8,1]]},"references-count":9,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,8,1]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/1.3122599","ISSN":["0021-8979","1089-7550"],"issn-type":[{"type":"print","value":"0021-8979"},{"type":"electronic","value":"1089-7550"}],"published-other":{"date-parts":[[2009,8,1]]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2009,8,1]]},"article-number":"034902"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,30]],"date-time":"2026-08-30T15:13:17Z","timestamp":1788102797242,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":12,"publisher":"American Vacuum Society","issue":"4","content-domain":{"domain":["pubs.aip.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,7,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>The authors analyze the feature filling phenomena for step and flash imprint lithography (SFIL) via diffusion of a gas, entrapped in the features, through liquid imprint resist. The model and simulation for the dynamics of feature filling including gas dissolution during the SFIL imprint step is presented. Several factors including the gas concentration profile across the liquid resist drop, the filling progression, and the total filling time for different pattern configurations are investigated to quantify feature filling. Simulation results show that initial filling is pressure controlled and very rapid [\u223cO(1ms)]. The rest of the feature filling is diffusion controlled, but fast enough [\u223cO(1s)] to conclude that diffusion of entrapped gas is not a cause for nonfilling of features. Also, the result that the smaller size features fill faster than the larger ones (with the same depth) makes SFIL the prime contender for high resolution and high throughput next generation lithography.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1116\/1.3147212","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2009,7,18]],"date-time":"2009-07-18T08:17:31Z","timestamp":1247905051000},"page":"1926-1932","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/aip-crossmark-policy-page","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":23,"title":["Feature filling modeling for step and flash imprint lithography"],"prefix":"10.1116","volume":"27","author":[{"given":"Siddharth","family":"Chauhan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"The University of Texas at Austin Department of Chemical Engineering, , 1 University Station CO400, Austin, Texas 78712"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Frank","family":"Palmieri","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The University of Texas at Austin Department of Chemical Engineering, , 1 University Station CO400, Austin, Texas 78712"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Roger T.","family":"Bonnecaze","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The University of Texas at Austin Department of Chemical Engineering, , 1 University Station CO400, Austin, Texas 78712"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"C. Grant","family":"Willson","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The University of Texas at Austin Department of Chemical Engineering, , 1 University Station CO400, Austin, Texas 78712"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"20","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2009,7,15]]},"reference":[{"key":"2023070922322083900_c1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"379","DOI":"10.1117\/12.351155","volume":"3676","year":"1999","journal-title":"Proc. SPIE"},{